# HiFi — paths Claude should never read directly.
#
# NOTE ON MECHANISM: Claude Code does not natively consume .claudeignore.
# The rules that actually take effect are the `permissions.deny` Read()
# entries in .claude/settings.json, which mirror this file one-for-one.
# This file is kept as the human-readable statement of intent (and is
# honoured by some other tools), so edit BOTH when changing the policy.
#
# Rationale: `data/` alone is 264 GB, of which 260 GB is a binary vector
# store. None of it is readable as text; a single accidental Read of a
# .lance fragment or a LoRA shard costs more tokens than a full source
# audit. Inspecting these artifacts is legitimate — but through pyarrow /
# lancedb / mlx in Bash, which summarises, not through the Read tool,
# which dumps.

# --- Binary data stores (260 GB) ---
# Only the binary fragments. The *.lance directory names themselves are NOT
# ignored: querying the store through lancedb in Bash is a core audit workflow
# (it is how the empty hifi-eval-episodes table was found), and a blanket
# `**/*.lance` rule blocks those Bash paths too.
data/knowledge.lance/**/data/
**/*.manifest
**/_versions/
**/_transactions/

# --- Model weights: LoRA adapters, checkpoints (3.6 GB) ---
data/adapters/
**/*.safetensors
**/*.gguf
**/*.npz
**/*.bin
**/*.pt
**/*.pth
**/*.ckpt

# --- Columnar / binary datasets: read via pyarrow, never as text ---
**/*.parquet
**/*.arrow
**/*.feather
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.pkl
**/*.pickle
**/*.h5

# --- Environments and caches ---
.venv/
venvs/
**/__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.codebase-memory/
node_modules/

# --- Secrets ---
.env
.env.*
docker/langfuse/.env

# --- Rendered / generated output, not source ---
data/tearsheets/
**/*.html
**/*.png
**/*.jpg
**/*.jpeg
**/*.pdf
**/*.zip
**/*.tar.gz

# --- OS noise ---
.DS_Store

# --- Deliberately NOT ignored ---
# data/live/**, data/runs/**, data/walkforward/**  : JSON decision sidecars,
#   the primary evidence for the Phase 16 audit trail. Must stay readable.
# data/macro/, data/market/                        : parquet, already covered
#   by the *.parquet rule; directory listings stay available.
# notebooks/*.ipynb                                : large, but they are the
#   deliverable. Prefer scripts/build_phase16_report_notebook.py over
#   reading the rendered notebook.
